<title>NEW ZEALAND: Canadian company buys into Direct Capital.</title>
<headline>Canadian company buys into Direct Capital.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Emerald Capital has acquired 7.1 million shares, or 8.35 percent, of listed New Zealand investment company Direct Capital from AMP, according to substantial security holder notices released to the New Zealand Stock Exchange on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Emerald is the New Zealand investment arm of Canadian investment company Gardiner Group Capital.</p>
<p>A Direct Capital spokesman confirmed the stake sold by AMP was the same purchased by Emerald, which has an office in Auckland.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
